" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">5.0 cm</text><text x="200" y="20" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">E = 1.0 × 10⁴ V m⁻¹</text><line x1="20" y1="110" x2="79.7" y2="110" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="86,110 77.8,113.8 77.8,106.2" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke:none"/><text x="22" y="96" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">2.0 × 10⁷ m s⁻¹</text><polyline points="90,110 97.3,110 104.7,109.8 112,109.6 119.3,109.3 126.7,108.8 134,108.3 141.3,107.7 148.7,107 156,106.2 163.3,105.3 170.7,104.4 178,103.3 185.3,102.1 192.7,100.9 200,99.5 207.3,98.1 214.7,96.5 222,94.9 229.3,93.2 236.7,91.3 244,89.4 251.3,87.4 258.7,85.3 266,83.1 273.3,80.8 280.7,78.5 288,76 295.3,73.4 302.7,70.8 310,68" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke-dasharray:6 4"/></svg>', 'Electrons moving at 2.0 × 10⁷ m s⁻¹ enter midway between plates 5.0 cm long with a field of 1.0 × 10⁴ V m⁻¹ and are deflected towards the positive plate.'),
('81e4ed3c-45a1-5f7a-b883-0534ec1d8ad9', '3fd36cc2-d7e7-4424-b4b5-11a4a8b7ac04', '932c79b4-ef68-44f7-9381-87d5ddebfa17', 'a-level', '25.5', '9702 coursebook 25.5 · Discovering the electron', 34, 34, 'An oil drop carries a charge of 8.0 × 10⁻¹⁹ C. How many excess electrons does it carry? Take e = 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ C.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '5', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'N = Q/e = 8.0 × 10⁻¹⁹ ÷ 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ = 5.0. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: N = Q/e. C1: whole number. A1: N = 5.0.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('6cb59acf-d6bb-58fb-9000-b554d7cca80e', '3fd36cc2-d7e7-4424-b4b5-11a4a8b7ac04', '932c79b4-ef68-44f7-9381-87d5ddebfa17', 'a-level', '25.5', '9702 coursebook 25.5 · Discovering the electron', 35, 35, 'How did combining Millikan''s and Thomson''s results give the mass of the electron?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'Millikan found e and Thomson found e/m, so m = e ÷ (e/m)', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Each experiment alone gives only e or e/m. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: e from Millikan. C1: e/m from Thomson. A1: C (Millikan found e and Thomson found e/m, so m = e ÷ (e/m)).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('87d4a581-2b73-5131-942a-48d863eb99e4', '3fd36cc2-d7e7-4424-b4b5-11a4a8b7ac04', '932c79b4-ef68-44f7-9381-87d5ddebfa17', 'a-level', '25.5', '9702 coursebook 25.5 · Discovering the electron', 36, 36, 'Using classical mechanics, calculate the speed of electrons accelerated from rest through 5.0 kV, as a percentage of the speed of light. Take e/m = 1.76 × 10¹¹ C kg⁻¹. Take c = 3.00 × 10⁸ m s⁻¹.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '13.98', '%', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'v = √(2 × 1.76 × 10¹¹ × 5000) = 4.20 × 10⁷ m s⁻¹. Percentage = 4.195 × 10⁷ ÷ 3.00 × 10⁸ × 100 = 14.0 %. Mark scheme (4 marks). C1: v = √(2(e/m)V). C1: ÷ c. C1: percentage. A1: percentage = 14.0%.', 4, NULL, NULL),
('b14c352e-74ba-5a54-824a-a4f44a034a98', '3fd36cc2-d7e7-4424-b4b5-11a4a8b7ac04', '932c79b4-ef68-44f7-9381-87d5ddebfa17', 'a-level', '25.5', '9702 coursebook 25.5 · Discovering the electron', 37, 37, 'An electron gun accelerates a beam of 0.20 mA through 2.0 kV. Calculate the power delivered to the screen.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.4', 'W', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'P = IV = 0.20 × 10⁻³ × 2.0 × 10³ = 0.40 W. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: each coulomb gains V joules. C1: P = IV. A1: P = 0.40 W.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('ae04cf51-5193-5a2f-ba55-348495bfa5c3', '3fd36cc2-d7e7-4424-b4b5-11a4a8b7ac04', '932c79b4-ef68-44f7-9381-87d5ddebfa17', 'a-level', '25.5', '9702 coursebook 25.5 · Discovering the electron', 38, 38, 'In a fine-beam tube, the beam forms a complete circle only when the magnetic field is at right angles to the beam. What happens if the field is at an angle?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'The beam follows a helix', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'The velocity component along the field is unaffected. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: parallel component unchanged. C1: helix. A1: A (The beam follows a helix).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('80bbe4a9-e023-5f29-9176-8e6283418482', '3fd36cc2-d7e7-4424-b4b5-11a4a8b7ac04', '932c79b4-ef68-44f7-9381-87d5ddebfa17', 'a-level', '25.5', '9702 coursebook 25.5 · Discovering the electron', 39, 39, 'Electrons accelerated through 250 V follow a circle of radius 6.0 cm in a field of 0.90 mT. Calculate e/m, in units of 10¹¹ C kg⁻¹.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '1.715', '10¹¹ C kg⁻¹', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'e/m = 2V/(B²r²) = 2 × 250 ÷ ((0.90 × 10⁻³)² × 0.060²) = 1.71 × 10¹¹ C kg⁻¹. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: e/m = 2V/(B²r²). C1: value. A1: e/m = 1.71 × 10¹¹ C kg⁻¹.', 3, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 260" role="img" aria-labelledby="fga1d1522f-t fga1d1522f-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fga1d1522f-t">Electron circle</title><desc id="fga1d1522f-d">Electrons accelerated through 250 V follow a circle of radius 6.0 cm in a uniform 0.90 mT field.</desc><line x1="30" y1="27.5" x2="38" y2="35.5" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="30" y1="35.5" x2="38" y2="27.5" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="30" y1="62.5" x2="38" y2="70.5" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="30" y1="70.5" x2="38" y2="62.5" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="30" y1="97.5" x2="38" y2="105.5" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="30" y1="105.5" x2="38" y2="97.5" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="30" y1="132.5" x2="38" y2="140.5" style="stroke:var(--fig-mut