;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke-dasharray:6 4"/><polygon points="356,105 348.7,108.4 348.7,101.6" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke:none"/><polygon points="374,50 377,56.3 371,56.3" style="fill:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke:none"/><line x1="374" y1="54.9" x2="374" y2="155.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="374,160 371,153.7 377,153.7" style="fill:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke:none"/><text x="380" y="105" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">3.0 cm</text><text x="120" y="198" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">p.d. 1500 V</text><line x1="120" y1="214" x2="128" y2="222" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="120" y1="222" x2="128" y2="214" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="136" y="218" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">B = 1.5 mT</text></svg>', 'Plates 3.0 cm apart with a p.d. of 1500 V and a magnetic field of 1.5 mT; electrons of one speed pass straight through.'),
('154af481-0d8d-56a2-a847-026004b4c43a', '3fd36cc2-d7e7-4424-b4b5-11a4a8b7ac04', '932c79b4-ef68-44f7-9381-87d5ddebfa17', 'a-level', '25.5', '9702 coursebook 25.5 · Discovering the electron', 42, 42, 'Why must the cathode of an electron gun be heated?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'To give electrons enough energy to escape from the metal surface', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Electrons need energy at least equal to the work function to leave the metal. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: energy to escape. C1: thermionic emission. A1: B (To give electrons enough energy to escape from the metal surface).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('6f53195f-2526-571e-bcf3-8dfc530193bb', '3fd36cc2-d7e7-4424-b4b5-11a4a8b7ac04', '932c79b4-ef68-44f7-9381-87d5ddebfa17', 'a-level', '25.5', '9702 coursebook 25.5 · Discovering the electron', 43, 43, 'In a fine-beam tube with a fixed field of 1.0 mT, the radius r is measured for different accelerating p.d.s V: V/V = 150, 200, 250, 300 and r/cm = 4.13, 4.77, 5.33, 5.84. (a) Show that r² = 2V/((e/m)B²). (b) Calculate the gradient of a graph of r² against V using the first and last points. (c) Calculate e/m, in units of 10¹¹ C kg⁻¹. Give only the answer to (c).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '1.76', '10¹¹ C kg⁻¹', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) eV = ½mv² and r = mv/(eB) give r² = 2mV/(eB²) = 2V/((e/m)B²). (b) Gradient = (0.0584² − 0.0413²) ÷ (300 − 150) = 1.14 × 10⁻⁵ m² V⁻¹. (c) e/m = 2 ÷ (B² × gradient) = 2 ÷ ((1.0 × 10⁻³)² × 1.137 × 10⁻⁵) = 1.76 × 10¹¹ C kg⁻¹. Mark scheme (6 marks). B1: r² expression. C1: r in m. C1: gradient. M1: e/m = 2/(B² × gradient). C1: value. A1: e/m = 1.76 × 10¹¹ C kg⁻¹.', 6, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 410" role="img" aria-labelledby="fged5d9e26-t fged5d9e26-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fged5d9e26-t">Radius against p.d.</title><desc id="fged5d9e26-d">Table and graph of the radius of the electron circle against accelerating p.d. at 1.0 mT: V = 150, 200, 250, 300 V give r = 4.13, 4.77, 5.33, 5.84 cm, plotted as points.</desc><g transform="translate(0,0)"><rect x="136.7" y="8" width="126.5" height="140" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="136.7" y="8" width="126.5" height="28" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="166.1" y="22" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:600">V / V</text><text x="229.4" y="22" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:600">r / cm</text><line x1="195.4" y1="8" x2="195.4" y2="148" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="136.7" y1="36" x2="263.3" y2="36" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="166.1" y="50" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">150</text><text x="229.4" y="50" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">4.13</text><line x1="136.7" y1="64" x2="263.3" y2="64" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="166.1" y="78" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">200</text><text x="229.4" y="78" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">4.77</text><line x1="136.7" y1="92" x2="263.3" y2="92" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="166.1" y="106" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">250</text><text x="229.4" y="106" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">5.33</text><line x1="136.7" y1="120" x2="263.3" y2="120" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="166.1" y="134" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">300</text><text x="229.4" y="134" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">5.84</text></g><g transform="translate(0,160)"><line x1="24" y1="34" x2="24" y2="202" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="135.9" y1="34" x2="135.9" y2="202" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="247.8" y1="34" x2="247.8" y2="202" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="359.6" y1="34" x2="359.6" y2="202" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="24" y1="202" x2="382" y2="202" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="24" y1="154" x2="382" y2="154" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="24" y1="106" x2="382" y2="106" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="24" y1="58" x2="382" y2="58" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="24" y1="202" x2="388" y2="202" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="24" y1="202" x2="24" y2="28" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="392,202 385.7,205 385.7,199" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><polygon points="24,24 27,30.3 21,30.3" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><line x1="24" y1="202" x2="24" y2="206" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="24" y="214" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">0</text><line x1="135.9" y1="202" x2="135.9" y2="206" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="135.9" y="2