-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="187.8" y1="106.9" x2="195.8" y2="98.9" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="243.8" y1="83.5" x2="251.8" y2="91.5" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="243.8" y1="91.5" x2="251.8" y2="83.5" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="299.7" y1="70.1" x2="307.7" y2="78.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="299.7" y1="78.1" x2="307.7" y2="70.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="355.6" y1="57.8" x2="363.6" y2="65.8" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="355.6" y1="65.8" x2="363.6" y2="57.8" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/></g></svg>', 'Table and graph of the radius of the electron circle against accelerating p.d. at 1.0 mT: V = 150, 200, 250, 300 V give r = 4.13, 4.77, 5.33, 5.84 cm, plotted as points.'),
('57b3cdd1-1b23-570d-a337-9ad553ec7341', '3fd36cc2-d7e7-4424-b4b5-11a4a8b7ac04', '932c79b4-ef68-44f7-9381-87d5ddebfa17', 'a-level', '25.5', '9702 coursebook 25.5 · Discovering the electron', 44, 44, 'In a Thomson-type experiment, plates 2.0 cm apart with a p.d. of 400 V and a field of 0.50 mT leave the beam undeflected. With the magnetic field switched off, the beam is deflected by 3.96 mm over the 6.0 cm length of the plates. (a) Calculate the speed of the electrons. (b) Show that e/m = 2yv²/(EL²). (c) Calculate e/m, in units of 10¹¹ C kg⁻¹. Give only the answer to (c).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '1.76', '10¹¹ C kg⁻¹', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) E = 400 ÷ 0.020 = 2.0 × 10⁴ V m⁻¹; v = E/B = 2.0 × 10⁴ ÷ 0.50 × 10⁻³ = 4.0 × 10⁷ m s⁻¹. (b) y = ½(e/m)E(L/v)², so e/m = 2yv²/(EL²). (c) e/m = 2 × 3.96 × 10⁻³ × (4.0 × 10⁷)² ÷ (2.0 × 10⁴ × 0.060²) = 1.76 × 10¹¹ C kg⁻¹. Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: E = V/d. C1: v = E/B. M1: y = ½at² with a = (e/m)E. B1: rearranged. C1: value. A1: e/m = 1.76 × 10¹¹ C kg⁻¹.', 6, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 220" role="img" aria-labelledby="fgfd47fa68-t fgfd47fa68-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fgfd47fa68-t">Thomson-type experiment</title><desc id="fgfd47fa68-d">Plates 2.0 cm apart and 6.0 cm long with a p.d. of 400 V. With the magnetic field off, the beam is deflected by 3.96 mm over the length of the plates.</desc><rect x="90" y="42" width="220" height="8" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="90" y="170" width="220" height="8" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="78" y="46" font-size="14" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:600">+</text><text x="78" y="174" font-size="14" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:600">−</text><line x1="110" y1="56" x2="110" y2="159.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="110,164 107,157.7 113,157.7" style="fill:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke:none"/><line x1="140" y1="56" x2="140" y2="159.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="140,164 137,157.7 143,157.7" style="fill:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke:none"/><line x1="170" y1="56" x2="170" y2="159.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="170,164 167,157.7 173,157.7" style="fill:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke:none"/><line x1="200" y1="56" x2="200" y2="159.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="200,164 197,157.7 203,157.7" style="fill:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke:none"/><line x1="230" y1="56" x2="230" y2="159.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="230,164 227,157.7 233,157.7" style="fill:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke:none"/><line x1="260" y1="56" x2="260" y2="159.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="260,164 257,157.7 263,157.7" style="fill:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke:none"/><line x1="290" y1="56" x2="290" y2="159.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="290,164 287,157.7 293,157.7" style="fill:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke:none"/><polygon points="332,50 335,56.3 329,56.3" style="fill:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke:none"/><line x1="332" y1="54.9" x2="332" y2="165.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="332,170 329,163.7 335,163.7" style="fill:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke:none"/><text x="338" y="110" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">2.0 cm</text><polygon points="90,196 96.3,193 96.3,199" style="fill:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke:none"/><line x1="94.9" y1="196" x2="305.1" y2="196" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="310,196 303.7,199 303.7,193" style="fill:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke:none"/><text x="200" y="208" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">6.0 cm</text><text x="200" y="20" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">p.d. 400 V</text><line x1="20" y1="110" x2="79.7" y2="110" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="86,110 77.8,113.8 77.8,106.2" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke:none"/><text x="22" y="96" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">electrons</text><polyline points="90,110 97.3,110 104.7,109.8 112,109.6 119.3,109.3 126.7,108.8 134,108.3 141.3,107.7 148.7,107 156,106.2 163.3,105.3 170.7,104.4 178,103.3 185.3,102.1 192.7,100.9 200,99.5 207.3,98.1 214.7,96.5 222,94.9 229.3,93.2 236.7,91.3 244,89.4 251.3,87.4 258.7,85.3 266,83.1 273.3,80.8 280.7,78.5 288,76 295.3,73.4 302.7,70.8 310,68" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke-dasharray:6 4"/></svg>', 'Plates 2.0 cm apart and 6.0 cm long with a p.d. of 400 V. With the magnetic field off, the beam is deflected by 3.96 mm over the length of the plates.'),
('43743c2c-29f6-5575-82c0-e4dd7a5510b1', '3fd36cc2-d7e7-4424-b4b5-11a4a8b7ac04', '932c79b4-ef68-44f7-9381-87d5ddebfa17', 'a-level', '25.5', '9702 coursebook 25.5 · Discovering the electron', 45, 45, 'Classical formulas for electron speed become inaccurate at high speeds. (a) Calculate the accelerating p.d. at which the classical speed of an electron would be 0.10c, in kV. Take e/m = 1.76 × 10¹¹ C kg⁻¹. (b) Suggest why a much higher p.d. is needed to reach 0.99c. Give only the answer to (a). Take c = 3.00 × 10⁸ m s⁻¹.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '2.557 kV', 'kV', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) v = 3.0 × 10⁷ m s⁻¹; V = v²/(2e/m) = (3.0 × 10⁷)² ÷ (2 × 1.76 × 10¹¹) = 2560 V. In kV: 2557 ÷ 1000 = 2.56. (b) Near c the electron''s effective mass grows and extra energy produces less and less increase in speed; it can never reach c. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: v = 0.10c. C1: V = v²/(2e/m). C1: conversion. B1: relativistic effects near c. A1: V = 2.56 kV.', 5, NULL, NULL),
('0b5de871-9af3-52cc-b453-c8b3953075b8', '3fd36cc2-d7e7-4424-b4b5-11a4a8b7ac04', '932c79b4-ef68-44f7-9381-87d5ddebfa17', 'a-level', '25.5', '9702 coursebook 25.5 · Discovering the electron', 46, 46, 'Thomson found that e/m for cathode-ray particles was 1.76 × 10¹¹ C kg⁻¹, while for hydrogen ions in electrolysis it was 9.58 × 10⁷ C kg⁻¹. (a) Calculate the ratio of the two values. (b) Assuming equal charges, state what this ratio means. (c) Use e = 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ C to find the mass of the cathode-ray particle. Give only the answer to (a).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '1837', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) Ratio = 1.76 × 10¹¹ ÷ 9.58 × 10⁷ = 1840. (b) The particle has about 1/1840 of the mass of a hydrogen ion. (c) m = 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ ÷ 1.76 × 10¹¹ = 9.09 × 10⁻³¹ kg. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: ratio. B1: mass ratio for equal charge. C1: m = e/(e/m). C1: value. A1: ratio = 1840.', 5, NULL, NULL),
('4a8c7b17-1449-5f0d-8cfe-c1174567070b', '3fd36cc2-d7e7-4424-b4b5-11a4a8b7ac04', '932c79b4-ef68-44f7-9381-87d5ddebfa17', 'a-level', '25.5', '9702 coursebook 25.5 · Discovering the electron', 47, 47, 'An oil drop of mass 9.6 × 10⁻¹⁵ kg is held stationary between plates 1.0 cm apart when the p.d. is 980 V. (a) Calculate the charge on the drop. (b) Calculate the number of excess electrons. (c) Explain how many such measurements showed that charge is quantised. Give only the answer to (b). Take g = 9.81 m s⁻² and e = 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ C.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '6.006', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) QV/d = mg, so Q = 9.6 × 10⁻¹⁵ × 9.81 × 0.010 ÷ 980 = 9.61 × 10⁻¹⁹ C. (b) N = 9.610 × 10⁻¹⁹ ÷ 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ = 6.01. (c) Every drop''s charge was a whole-number multiple of the same value, 1.6 × 10⁻¹⁹ C. Mark scheme (5 marks). M1: QV/d = mg. C1: Q. C1: N = Q/e. B1: all multiples of e. A1: N = 6.01.', 5, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 360 230" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg4add3a1b-t fg4add3a1b-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg4add3a1b-t">Oil drop held stationary</title><desc id="fg4add3a1b-d">An oil drop of mass 9.6 × 10⁻¹⁵ kg held stationary between horizontal plates 1.0 cm apart with a p.d. of 980 V: the upward electric force balances its weight.</desc><rect x="70" y="42" width="220" height="8" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="70" y="170" width="220" height="8" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="58" y="46" font-size="14" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:700">+</text><text x="58" y="174" font-size="14" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:700">−</text><circle cx="180" cy="110" r="7" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="180" y1="101" x2="180" y2="66.3" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="180,60 183.8,68.2 176.2,68.2" style="fill:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke:none"/><text x="188" y="70" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8)">electric force</text><line x1="180" y1="119" x2="180" y2="153.7" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="180,160 176.2,151.8 183.8,151.8" style="fill:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke:none"/><text x="188" y="150" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8)">weight</text><text x="166" y="110" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309)">9.6 × 10⁻¹⁵ kg</text><polygon points="312,50 315,56.3 309,56.3" style="fill:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke:none"/><line x1="312" y1="54.9" x2="312" y2="165.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="312,170 309,163.7 315,163.7" style="fill:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke:none"/><text x="318" y="110" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">1.0 cm</text><text x="180" y="24" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">p.d. 980 V</text></svg>', 'An oil drop of mass 9.6 × 10⁻¹⁵ kg held stationary between horizontal plates 1.0 cm apart with a p.d. of 980 V: the upward electric force balances its weight.'),
('7909402b-01af-5bbc-85c3-3f8edf301bcf', '3fd36cc2-d7e7-4424-b4b5-11a4a8b7ac04', '932c79b4-ef68-44f7-9381-87d5ddebfa17', 'a-level', '25.5', '9702 coursebook 25.5 · Discovering the electron', 48, 48, 'An electron gun has an accelerating p.d. of 4.0 kV and a beam current of 2.5 mA. (a) Calculate the number of electrons emitted per second. (b) Calculate the speed of the electrons, taking e/m = 1.76 × 10¹¹ C kg⁻¹. (c) Calculate the power delivered by the beam. (d) Suggest what happens to this energy at the screen. Give only the answer to (b). Take e = 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ C.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '3.752e7', 'm s⁻¹', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) N = 2.5 × 10⁻³ ÷ 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ = 1.56 × 10¹⁶ s⁻¹. (b) v = √(2 × 1.76 × 10¹¹ × 4000) = 3.75 × 10⁷ m s⁻¹. (c) P = IV = 2.5 × 10⁻³ × 4000 = 10 W. (d) Most becomes internal energy (heating) of the screen; a little becomes light. Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: N = I/e. C1: v = √(2(e/m)V). C1: P = IV. B1: heating and light. C1: value. A1: v = 3.75 × 10⁷ m s⁻¹.', 6, NULL, NULL),
('0089dd3d-7638-55bd-9fa4-30e8e628c513', '3fd36cc2-d7e7-4424-b4b5-11a4a8b7ac04', '932c79b4-ef68-44f7-9381-87d5ddebfa17', 'a-level', '25.5', '9702 coursebook 25.5 · Discovering the electron', 49, 49, 'In a fine-beam tube, electrons follow a circle of radius 6.0 cm. The accelerating p.d. and the magnetic field are then both doubled. (a) Show that r ∝ √V/B. (b) Calculate the new radius, in cm. Give only the answer to (b).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '4.243 cm', 'cm', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) r = √(2mV/e)/B, so r ∝ √V/B. (b) r = 6.0 × √2 ÷ 2 = 4.24 cm. Mark scheme (5 marks). M1: r = √(2mV/e)/B. B1: proportionality. C1: factor √2/2. C1: value. A1: r = 4.24 cm.', 5, NULL, NULL),
('354e9ba4-6422-54af-9629-972644fa00d9', '3fd36cc2-d7e7-4424-b4b5-11a4a8b7ac04', '932c79b4-ef68-44f7-9381-87d5ddebfa17', 'a-level', '25.5', '9702 coursebook 25.5 · Discovering the electron', 50, 50, 'Electrons moving at 2.0 × 10⁷ m s⁻¹ cross a region 3.0 cm wide containing a field of 1.0 mT and are deflected through 15.3°. (a) Show that the radius of their path in the field is r = (width)/sin θ. (b) Calculate r. (c) Calculate e/m, in units of 10¹¹ C kg⁻¹. Give only the answer to (c).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '1.759', '10¹¹ C kg⁻¹', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) The electron follows an arc; the geometry of a circle crossing a strip of width d gives sin θ = d/r. (b) r = 0.030 ÷ sin 15.3° = 0.114 m. (c) e/m = v/(Br) = 2.0 × 10⁷ ÷ (1.0 × 10⁻³ × 0.1137) = 1.76 × 10¹¹ C kg⁻¹. Mark scheme (6 marks). B1: geometry. C1: r. M1: e/m = v/(Br). C1: substitution. C1: value. A1: e/m = 1.76 × 10¹¹ C kg⁻¹.', 6, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 240" role="img" aria-labelledby="fgc3cf3b37-t fgc3cf3b37-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fgc3cf3b37-t">Beam crossing a field region</title><desc id="fgc3cf3b37-d">Electrons moving at 2.0 × 10⁷ m s⁻¹ cross a region 3.0 cm wide containing a uniform 1.0 mT field and leave deflected through 15.3°.</desc><rect x="150" y="14" width="110" height="190" rx="0" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke-dasharray:5 4"/><line x1="164.3" y1="25.8" x2="172.3" y2="33.8" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="164.3" y1="33.8" x2="172.3" y2="25.8" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="164.3" y1="57.5" x2="172.3" y2="65.5" style="stroke:var(--fig-mu